Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:20:00 +0300
Subject: Default support8bpp to system so the 8bpp-optimized blitter is used

With support8bpp at its default "no", the blitter that OpenTTD guesses
at start and settles on after the NewGRFs load is 32bpp-anim, even for
an 8bpp base set such as OpenGFX. On the PS3 (a 3.2 GHz in-order PPE
drawing 1920x1080) the 32bpp blit and its animation buffer cost most of
a frame: our savegame of 1962 ran at 11 fps with 32bpp-anim and 34-43
fps with 8bpp-optimized through the OpenGL driver, the picture the
same. "system" makes the guess 8bpp and keeps the NewGRF check: a
NewGRF that asks for 32bpp, or font anti-aliasing, still switches to a
32bpp blitter. A config that sets support8bpp or blitter explicitly,
and the -b option, are unchanged (32bpp-anim stays selectable).

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/table/settings/misc_settings.ini b/src/table/settings/misc_settings.ini
--- a/src/table/settings/misc_settings.ini
+++ b/src/table/settings/misc_settings.ini
@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@ cat      = SC_BASIC
 name     = ""support8bpp""
 type     = SLE_UINT8
 var      = _support8bpp
-def      = 0
+def      = 1
 max      = 2
 full     = _support8bppmodes
 cat      = SC_BASIC
